Revision history for Term::Fabulous

0.01    Unreleased
        - Term::Fabulous::Widget::Table shows rows of Perl hashes in
          columns: widths that fit, grow, are fixed or a percentage,
          with limits; wrapping and rows as high as their tallest cell;
          mutators for the display text (Table::Mutator: dates, numbers,
          percentages, sizes, durations, flags, lookups); any widget as
          a cell, kept across data changes with update_cell; sorting by
          one or several columns by the user or from Perl, with string,
          natural, number, date or custom comparisons; filtering with a
          filter row whose expressions read text, numbers and date spans
          (">=100", "2024-05", "10..20"), named Table::Filter objects
          with all/any/not, on the raw value or the display text, and a
          search over the visible columns; groups by one or more
          columns with labels of your own; trees of nested rows; pages
          with a pager; a cursor and none, single or multiple selection
          with a selection column; a column chooser; colors, stripes and
          lines per table, column, row and cell, joined into one grid,
          and frames in the block styles Outer, Inner and Thick, which
          enclose colored cells cleanly;
          full keyboard and mouse use; KDL properties. User actions
          fire the new events CursorMove, SelectionChange, RowActivate,
          SortChange, FilterChange, PageChange, Expand, Collapse and
          ColumnsChange; changes from Perl fire none. The data and the
          view live in Table::Model, which has no widgets. Documented
          by feature with a feature index, a TABLES chapter in the
          Manual and the Cookbook, examples/widgets/table.pl,
          examples/table-directory.pl and examples/table-files.pl
        - Enum::BorderStyle junction gives the glyph where lines of any
          styles meet; Role::HasBorderStyle gains border_corners (corner
          glyphs of your own) and outer_border_sides (sides drawn on the
          background outside the widget), used by Render::Border
        - Text gains bold, italic and underline (also in KDL); the
          terminal grid emits italic
        - Render gains after_draw, a one-shot callback after the next
          frame. A change now costs one frame: the drawn revision is the
          one the layout started from, which removes a second frame
          after every interaction
        - Check gains sizing, which reads sizing strings such as
          'fit(0, 30)' or 'percent(25)'; KDL sizing and table column
          widths use it
        - Needs the matching Clay::UI (Grid spanning rows and shared
          columns, Preparable, laid_out_revision, scroll_state,
          scroll_to, bounding_box), List::Util 1.33 and Time::Local 1.30
        - Term::Fabulous::TextView lays out the text of the text
          inputs: visual rows with wrapping, the cursor's cell, the
          scroll position, the text position under a cell and moves by
          rows. TextField is a view of one row, TextArea one that may
          wrap; TextInput paints for both. Sideways scrolling has one
          rule for both: the view starts at a whole character of the
          cursor's line and scrolls no further than needed to fill it.
          TextInput's subclass interface shrinks to is_multi_line, view,
          paint, hides_text, display_cluster and apply_edit
          (scroll_to_cursor, position_at, clusters_between, columns_to,
          offset_at_column, paint_line_part, paint_placeholder and
          shows_placeholder are gone)
        - "Disabled" is Clay::UI's: the inputs, RadioGroup and Button
          compose Clay::UI::Role::Interaction::Disableable and
          Focusable directly, and Clay::UI derives can_focus, never
          presses a disabled widget and takes the focus away at once
          from a widget that is disabled or written can_focus(0). The
          derived state disabled shows in get_classes as
          state_disabled. Button gains disabled and disabled_color
          (also in KDL): a disabled button ignores clicks, Enter and
          Space and draws its border and its text in disabled_color.
          "Can this widget take the focus now" is asked in one place,
          Clay::UI's interaction->can_take_focus
        - Input widgets paint when a frame is drawn: setters record the
          value and call mark_changed, and the renderer calls the new
          Canvas hook refresh, where an input compares its paint key
          (its size, its own changes, focus, enabled, and what other
          widgets decide: a radio button's group, a dropdown list's
          colors and highlight, a text input's editor) and paints only
          when it changed. Fixes a disabled cursor button that left the
          focus look on the wrong radio button, an accent_color change
          that did not reach an open dropdown list, and a text field
          edited through $field->editor that stayed scrolled away from
          its cursor. Input->repaint, TextInput->cursor_moved,
          RadioGroup->repaint_buttons, Dropdown::List->repaint and the
          size_changed hook are gone; call mark_changed instead. A
          canvas reports a changed span only for cells that really
          changed, so clearing and drawing the same cells again sends
          nothing to the terminal. Editor->revision now counts changes
          of the text, the cursor and the selection; text_revision
          counts text changes
        - Widget properties are checked by one module,
          Term::Fabulous::Check, so every positive integer, string,
          boolean, single-column glyph and color is checked the same
          way and fails with one wording ("NAME must be a positive
          integer, got '0'"). Input colors are kept and returned as
          [r, g, b, a], like the colors of every widget
        - KDL properties are declared once per class:
          layout_properties is a class method returning name =>
          'scalar', 'boolean', 'color' or a parsing handler, and
          replaces boolean_layout_properties,
          structured_layout_properties, parse_node, parse_property and
          parse_generic; colors are declared, not recognized by a
          _color suffix. Term::Fabulous::Layout builds a widget with
          new( id => $id ) and then applies the layout node to the
          finished widget (apply_layout_node, apply_layout_settings);
          kdl_node is gone. Related values apply together in any order:
          a Slider's min, max and step (also new as set_range), a
          Dropdown's options before its value, a text input's
          max_length before its value
        - Term::Fabulous talks to the terminal only through a terminal
          object (Term::Fabulous::Role::Terminal), given to new as
          terminal: Term::Fabulous::Terminal::Termbox, the real terminal
          and the default (it also runs on other terminals through its
          input and output handles), or Term::Fabulous::Terminal::Memory,
          a terminal in memory for tests that queues keys by name
          (press_key), typed text, clicks, mouse events and resizes, and
          shows the screen as lines and cells. step is one turn of run
          without an event loop: it opens the terminal, reads and
          dispatches the queued input as run does, applies a resize at
          once and draws every due frame, returning how many; with
          paced => 1 and the new clock parameter it paces pointer motion
          like run. KeyPress->fields_for_name turns a key name back into
          termbox2's event fields. The renderer paints into one cell
          target object (cell_target) instead of seven target methods;
          Render::Target::Grid is a class that also formats its rows as
          text (row_text), and Render::Target::Termbox is replaced by
          Terminal::Termbox::Cells. The errors of opening the real
          terminal start with Term::Fabulous::Terminal::Termbox:
        - Term::Fabulous::Render::Frame works out once per frame what
          it paints: the paint order, the clip rect of every command
          and the cells every command paints. Drawing, canvas planning
          and hit-testing all read it. last_frame returns the Frame of
          the last frame (get_last_commands and get_last_clip_rects are
          gone), and it is complete even when painting died partway.
          Term::Fabulous::Render::Clip is gone; the painters' clip_rect
          comes from Term::Fabulous::Render. A border wider than one
          cell takes the mouse only on the cells it draws
        - Kitty keyboard protocol: run asks the terminal whether it
          speaks the protocol and switches it on (flags 1 and 4) until
          run returns; terminals without it are read as before, and
          Term::Fabulous->new( kitty_keyboard => 0 ) leaves it off.
          kitty_keyboard_active tells whether run uses it. Ctrl
          combinations get their own names (Ctrl+I, Ctrl+Shift+W,
          Ctrl+Enter), Alt+[ can be bound, the Super, Hyper and Meta
          modifiers and the keys F13 to F35, the keypad, the lock and
          media keys are reported. KeyPress gains main_key_name, which
          names the keypad keys after the main keyboard keys; the
          built-in widgets bind their keys with it.
          Term::Fabulous::Termbox gains tf_kitty_keyboard_query, the
          TF_KEY_* kitty keys and TF_MOD_SUPER, TF_MOD_HYPER and
          TF_MOD_META; its input parser decodes CSI u key reports and
          modified function keys with any modifier
        - Inline mode: Term::Fabulous->new( inline => $rows ) draws the
          user interface into that many rows below the shell's output
          instead of taking over the screen, draws the final state and
          keeps it there when run returns, and finds the region again
          after a resize. It has no mouse support; the cookbook recipe
          "Ask for input below the shell's output" shows it.
          Term::Fabulous::Termbox gains tf_init_inline,
          tf_init_inline_rwfd, tf_cursor_position, tf_reset_attrs and
          tf_flush
        - Dialogs keep the keyboard to themselves: keys the widgets of
          an open dialog do not use stop at its backdrop instead of
          reaching the key bindings behind it; when the focused widget
          inside is disabled or removed, the backdrop takes the focus;
          Shift+Tab from the backdrop goes to the last widget; close
          works (and fires Close) after the program took the dialog out
          of the tree; an open dialog no longer keeps a dropped UI
          alive. An open Dropdown list floats over every z_index, so
          it works inside a dialog
        - can_focus and disabled no longer depend on their order: an
          input or radio group built with disabled #true takes the
          focus once it is enabled, and can_focus written while
          disabled counts once enabled
        - Wheel scrolling is explicit: a widget that scrolled itself
          calls use_wheel on the Mouse event; what listeners return no
          longer keeps a ScrollBox from scrolling. TextArea, Slider and
          the Dropdown list leave a notch they cannot use to the
          ScrollBox around them
        - Mouse events say which button a release released
          (released_button); only the left button's release ends a
          press
        - run fires Start from inside the running loop ($ui->loop works
          in Start listeners), stops on SIGHUP too, gives back the
          program's INT, TERM and HUP handlers, and dies with "the
          terminal was closed" at the end of the terminal input instead
          of spinning
        - A click where a widget was removed since the last frame no
          longer kills run; a resize that ends at the old size repaints
          the canvases; borders beside an unchanged canvas keep their
          colors; pointer motion alone draws at most every other frame
          while frames are slow
        - TextArea wraps only the lines an edit changed; a wide
          character after a carried word is no longer hidden; the space
          at which a full row wraps hangs instead of starting the next
          row. Editor undo steps keep the replaced text only
        - Text inputs: Shift+click extends the selection; a TextField
          with a mask copies and cuts nothing and moves and deletes by
          the whole text instead of by word
        - PixelCanvas draw_line and draw_circle cost no more than the
          canvas is wide or high, however far the shape reaches
        - tb_send sends bytes as they are (tf_readable_bytes is new);
          Button takes #null and "reverse" in KDL; classes is checked
        - Documentation with pictures: Term::Fabulous::Examples lists
          every example program with a screenshot; the overview below
          the SYNOPSIS of Term::Fabulous (and in README.md) shows the
          new examples/showcase.pl; every widget page shows a preview
          below its SYNOPSIS, taken from the new widget gallery in
          examples/widgets; the Cookbook, the Manual and the pages of
          WebColor, BorderStyle and Static show the matching programs
        - The complete programs of Term::Fabulous::Cookbook are shipped
          in examples-cookbook, one file per recipe; the Cookbook's code
          blocks are copies of the shipped files
        - Maintainer tools in tools/ (shipped, not installed): make docs
          copies the example programs into the POD and takes the
          screenshots again, reproducibly (each program runs in a pseudo
          terminal on a virtual clock in a fixed environment); make
          docs-check fails when either is out of date and runs before
          make release; tools/screenshot takes an SVG or PNG screenshot
          of any Term::Fabulous program
        - Frames are drawn only when something changed: a widget setter
          (Clay::UI::Revision), Clay::XS::set_scroll_position, input,
          a resize or $ui->invalidate.
          Widget classes of your own call mark_changed (or repaint)
          after changing drawn state
        - The terminal reports mouse movement without a button (mode
          1003): MouseMove events, hover that follows the pointer, and
          Shift, Alt and Ctrl in Mouse events. A horizontal wheel
          scrolls sideways (TF_KEY_MOUSE_WHEEL_LEFT/RIGHT). The SGR
          mouse reports and Alt+key are decoded by Term::Fabulous's own
          parser (tf_install_input_parser), so Alt+x, Alt+Enter and
          Alt plus an umlaut are key names of their own
        - A Start event with the terminal size is fired on the root when
          run opens the terminal, before the first frame
        - Button fires Activate for a click and for Enter or Space,
          draws its border in focus_border_color while focused and
          inverts its colors while pressed (pressed_background_color)
        - Widget::Dialog opens a box centered over the screen behind a
          dimming backdrop, keeps Tab inside, closes on Escape and
          fires Close; it can be opened again. Requires Clay::UI with
          re-attachable widgets (a removed widget can be added again)
        - KDL layouts: sizing takes "grow(MIN)", "grow(MIN, MAX)",
          "fit(MIN)" and "fit(MIN, MAX)"; Box has the new property
          nodes child_alignment x=... y=... and floating attach_to=...
          parent_id=... element=... parent=... offset_x=... offset_y=...
          z_index=... pointer_capture=... clip_to=...; Text has
          wrap_mode and text_alignment; Button has focus_border_color
          and pressed_background_color
        - Every container widget composes
          Clay::UI::Role::Layout::HasFloating and accepts a floating
          parameter and accessor
        - Widget::find_by_id and $ui->find_by_id find a widget (Text
          included) by its id, depth first
        - max_element_count raises Clay's element limit (8192 by
          default); a too-large tree dies with a message that names it
        - Border styles: Tab is gone (it was identical to Wide).
          Hidden now switches a side off: it draws nothing and takes
          no space, whatever the side's border_width; Blank still
          takes space and draws spaces
        - First version. Terminal UIs from Clay layouts, drawn with
          termbox2: Box, Text and Button widgets, border styles,
          truecolor rendering, KDL layout files and an IO::Async
          driven event loop with key, mouse and resize events
        - Term::Fabulous::Static renders a widget tree once, to text
          with optional ANSI truecolor, without opening the terminal.
          The render roles paint through a cell target role
          (Render::Target::Termbox for the terminal, Render::Target::Grid
          for memory) instead of calling termbox2 directly
        - termbox2 is compiled into the distribution as
          Term::Fabulous::Termbox (XS, 64-bit attributes, grapheme
          clusters); the Termbox and FFI::Platypus dependencies are
          gone. Text is measured with termbox2's own width functions,
          so emoji presentation sequences (U+FE0F), ZWJ sequences and
          flags take two columns
        - Term::Fabulous::Unicode remembers the grapheme clusters and
          the width of every text it has measured, so layout callbacks
          and drawing no longer segment the same strings on every frame
        - Scroll containers: the renderer honors Clay's scissor commands
          (Render::Clip), Widget::ScrollBox is a Box that scrolls, and
          the mouse wheel scrolls the box under the pointer by three
          rows per notch. Hit testing ignores content scrolled out of
          view
        - Tab and Shift-Tab move the keyboard focus after their KeyPress
        - Requires the Clay::UI interaction tracker: focus is read
          through $ui->interaction, and border_width is validated by
          Clay::UI when it is set
        - Widget::Canvas: a free-drawing buffer of grapheme clusters
          with any foreground and background color, sized by the layout
          (CanvasResize event). Frames keep the cells of canvases that
          did not move and that nothing covers (Render::Target::Mask),
          so only their changed cells are painted
        - Widget::PixelCanvas: a canvas of half-block pixels, two per
          cell, with pixel, rect, line and circle drawing. Canvas::cell_at
          and PixelCanvas::pixel_at map mouse events to cells and pixels
        - Input widgets: TextField, TextArea, Checkbox, RadioGroup with
          RadioButton, Dropdown and Slider, built on Widget::Input (a
          canvas that paints itself, takes the focus and sizes itself to
          its content) and fired Change events; TextField fires Submit.
          The text inputs share Term::Fabulous::Editor: grapheme-aware
          cursor movement, selection, word editing keys, undo and redo,
          and a clipboard. All of them can be built from KDL layouts
        - A left mouse press focuses the widget under the pointer (or its
          nearest focusable ancestor) and blurs when there is none
        - Clay gets the pointer at the center of its cell, so pressing the
          top row of a widget no longer also presses the widget above it
        - Event::KeyPress::key_name and text name keys for bindings
          ('Ctrl+Shift+Left', 'Enter', 'a'); Widget::Box::parse_property
          lets subclasses parse KDL properties of their own
        - Documentation: Term::Fabulous::Manual (user guide) and
          Term::Fabulous::Cookbook (recipes), reference documentation
          for every module, and the examples buttons-and-keys.pl,
          kdl-form.pl and custom-widget.pl
        - Translucent backgrounds: a background_color with an alpha from
          1 to 254 is blended with what lies below the widget. The new
          widget parameter glyphs_show_through decides whether the text
          and borders below stay visible, tinted, or are covered. The
          cell targets gained painted_cell to read a cell back
        - Term::Fabulous::Enum::WebColor holds the 148 CSS named colors
          as Term::Fabulous::Color objects (it was an empty placeholder)
        - Every widget color (background_color, border_color, the
          text_color of a Text widget) takes any Term::Fabulous::Color
          input, and Color->new reads a packed 0xRRGGBB integer. The
          rgba and hsla class methods read alpha like the string forms,
          and blend validates its arguments and rounds. KDL boolean
          properties accept only #true/#false (or 0/1), a second
          padding node merges, and the "unknown layout property" error
          lists the structured properties too. Boolean parameters are
          stored as 1 or 0, checkbox and radio labels stay in place when
          the mark changes, Static rejects unknown options, the
          constructors reject measure_text, key_name has no name for C1
          control characters, editor errors name the text input, and
          the editor clipboard can be read through an editor
        - Text widgets take character strings like everything else;
          UTF-8 bytes no longer have to be encoded for them. can_focus
          given to new is honored by the input widgets and RadioGroup,
          and disabled(0) restores it. A press and a release within one
          frame both reach Clay, so fast clicks press buttons. A wheel
          notch a widget handled (TextArea, Slider, the dropdown list)
          no longer also scrolls the ScrollBox around it; fire_event
          reports the outcome for that. A border_style_<side> parameter
          wins over border_style, as in KDL. Slider values keep the
          decimals of min and of tiny steps. TextInput drops its
          Shift+click branch, which termbox2 can never trigger, and
          examples/kdl-layout.pl starts again
